      "extract": "In this paper we wish to describe certain natural $4$-vector fields on quaternionic flag manifolds. In the context of the Poisson geometry, a bi-vector field is penultimate in the study of the geometry of the underlying manifold. Analogously, we make use of a $4$-vector field, closed under the Schouten bracket with itself, which we call a \\emph{quatrisson} structure, to reveal the internal structures of certain",
